  Interpretation: on the subcube family the best slope is w_heavy/(2d) = 9/50
  = 0.18 < 79/400 = 0.1975 (depth-1, heavy split). The ball code (non-subcube)
  beats every subcube tree; consistent with the BP1 conjecture whose extremal
  is the antipodal ball code. Refutation would require a NON-subcube tree
  with ratio > 79/400; depth-2 ball-outer + random-outer families checked in C.
